      }
    },
    {
      "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request modifies the qk_norm_rope_fusion pass to exclude the flashinfer-rope variant from the fusion patterns. This change serves as a workaround for a known issue in PyTorch Inductor's pattern matcher that occurs when custom operators mutate multiple tensor arguments sharing symbolic dimensions, a scenario encountered with DeepSeek-V3.2 sparse-MLA. I have no feedback to provide.",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/40910#pullrequestreview-4176797215",
      "id": 4176797215,
      "state": "COMMENTED",
      "submitted_at": "2026-04-26T10:10:25Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "gemini-code-assist[bot]"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Looks good overall, but a few questions:\n1. Does this only happen for flashinfer rope?\n2. Is this fusion relevant to Deepseek models? I thought it would only work for qwen.\n3. Could we get a minimal PyTorch repro, so this can be fixed on the pytorch side? If it's minimal enough we might even be able to get the fix in 2.12.\n\nThanks for fixing this.\n",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/40910#pullrequestreview-4177513777",
      "id": 4177513777,
      "state": "APPROVED",
